://scontent-sin6-2.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491818860_877756728422945_305704471306386766_n.png?_nc_cat=109&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=dEAZs2t4mjcQ7kNvwGxWw_F&_nc_oc=AdogUhnOYcHvWYlJFdhcnVkME0MW63AkcSoVnZ1h5Uobj8RdpN0YS9KSiVsV11orSI4&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sin6-2.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_Af9aAMSTebElc1Ub2HNZyKZ_fO6vR9109K3FLtBVezG8HA&oe=6A22F919"}, {"file_name": "5.png", "id": "862412696831084", "uri": "https://scontent-sin2-3.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491821725_862412700164417_4630813560218885361_n.png?_nc_cat=107&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=6tYB1d6G3-kQ7kNvwEdsuZt&_nc_oc=AdpOKAEhWGgBIXVJHEC8nQrUn_SPgzT5fDNdq8DRL2DnkmaFYT1iG2fuvswzIjNSJM8&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sin2-3.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_Af_uDtIRpQYcbtLmL_3o3o26ghRdNlgN4Nt_MMFzmc9K3w&oe=6A23020E"}, {"file_name": "6.png", "id": "923637530158794", "uri": "https://scontent-sin11-1.oculuscdn.com/v/t64.5771-25/491820855_923637533492127_5988481766482833666_n.png?_nc_cat=105&ccb=1-7&_nc_sid=6e7a0a&_nc_ohc=BAjzZkSIXH8Q7kNvwFGsHsg&_nc_oc=AdpvSEQupx2aFX4XDoFgMMExBOwwlmveP7jgKL9yNP9gm27XvDKTMx9TgCm8MzClWSY&_nc_zt=3&_nc_ht=scontent-sin11-1.oculuscdn.com&_nc_ss=7f20f&oh=00_Af9cIHJjxTnJkFVfa8G4O4x42CClBVTFTQl-eAtXPuBbGQ&oe=6A22D2F9"}], "video_trailer": null, "video_trailer_thumbnail": null, "display_name": "Vertex VR Video Player", "keywords": [], "long_description": " Vertex VR Video Player is a lightweight yet powerful VR video player designed for Meta Quest. It supports a wide range of video formats and projection types, including:\n\n  Projection modes:\n  - Flat screen (cinema-style virtual screen)\n  - 180\u00b0 and 360\u00b0 sphere projection\n  - Equi-Angular Cubemap (EAC) \u2014 compatible with videos downloaded from YouTube\n\n  Stereo formats:\n  - Side-by-Side (SBS) \u2014 half and full width\n  - Top-Bottom (TB) \u2014 half and full height\n  - Mono\n  - SBS Fisheye (equidistant projection)\n\n  Key features:\n  - High-quality rendering with bicubic upscaling, sRGB-correct color pipeline, and anti-banding dithering\n  - Multiple color profiles (Realism, Vivid, Teal & Orange, Vintage, PhotoReal, 3D)\n  - Adjustable video enhancement settings: sharpness, clarity, brightness, contrast, saturation, gamma, warmth, and depth effect\n  - Smooth playback mode with optimized buffering for stutter-free viewing\n  - Support for 4K and 8K video decoding\n  - Playback from internal storage and USB OTG devices (flash drives, microSD card readers, external HDDs via NTFS)\n  - Automatic detection of video type (180\u00b0/360\u00b0, SBS/TB) based on filename and resolution\n  - Intuitive VR menu with controller interaction \u2014 drag to pan, thumbstick to zoom\n  - Mirror mode, eye swap, and IPD offset adjustments\n\n  The app focuses on delivering the best possible video quality and smoothness while keeping the interface simple and easy to use. No account required, no internet connection needed \u2014 just load your videos and play.\n{1677380656960522}\n{1881898025800384}\n{1286088660090195}\n{1510923663604622}\n{2300424457109437}\n{1308594671284908}", "short_description": "Vertex VR Video Player \u2014 a high-quality VR video player for Meta Quest. Supports 180\u00b0 and 360\u00b0 SBS/TB videos, flat screen mode, and EAC (YouTube 360). Features bicubic upscaling, sRGB-correct colors, adjustable sharpness, clarity, contrast, saturation, and multiple color\n  profiles. Plays from internal storage and USB OTG (NTFS). Auto-detects video type. Simple interface, maximum quality."}]}, "developer_name": null, "developer_privacy_policy_url": "https://f1tt0n.github.io/vertex-privacy/privacy.html", "developer_terms_of_service_url": null, "publisher_name": "ANWAR", "support_website_url": null, "website_url": "https://f1tt0n.github.io/vertex-privacy/", "category": null, "comfort_rating": "COMFORTABLE_FOR_MOST", "comfort_tags": [], "context_category": {"id": "362692211442873", "context_category": "APPS"}, "context_topics": [{"id": "434961926215971"}], "external_subscription_type": "NOT_REQUIRED", "genres": [], "has_in_app_ads": null, "internet_connection": "NOT_REQUIRED", "play_area": "NO_MOVEMENT", "recommended_graphics": null, "recommended_memory_gb": null, "recommended_processor": null, "supported_in_app_languages": ["en"], "supported_input_devices": ["OCULUS_TOUCH"], "supported_player_modes": ["SITTING", "STANDING", "ROOM_SCALE"], "supported_tracking_modes": [], "user_interaction_modes": ["SINGLE_USER"], "id": "27125292510404479"}}]}, "scheduled_offers": {"count": 1, "nodes": [{"status": "PUBLISHED", "id": "790545066825215"}]}, "baseline_offer": {"id": "790545066825215"}, "is_approved": true, "firstOffer": {"nodes": [{"start_time": 1772909220, "status": "PUBLISHED", "id": "790545066825215"}]}, "liveChannel": {"nodes": [{"latest_supported_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "id": "28147896118144108", "version": "2.8"}, "id": "1252765963588051", "channel_name": "LIVE"}]}, "is_for_oculus_keys_only": false, "primary_binaries": {"nodes": [{"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "27125292497071147", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "28147896118144108"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1252765963588051"}]}, "change_log": "What's New in 2.8\n\nExternal Integration API\n- Other apps can now launch the player with full control over how the video plays.\n- New intent extras: projection_mode, stereo_mode, swap_eyes, start_position_ms, loop, no_ui, lock_input, auto_exit.\n- Use cases: deep-linking from a 2D companion app, embedding the renderer in kiosk/showcase apps, looping VR content with no UI.\n- Full documentation provided to integrators in EXTERNAL_INTEGRATION.md.\n\nBug fix\n- Auto-applied PhotoReal color profile is no longer forced for any video. Factory default is now neutral (matches Reset Enhance) for ALL videos including auto-detected 180. Lower-quality content no longer looks over-sharpened. Users can still pick PhotoReal manually in the Enhance panel.\n\nPreviously in 2.7\n\nCritical Fix\n- Fixed a hang where the player would never start a video after enabling 'Remember Settings' and restarting the app. Settings load and rendering pipeline are now decoupled, so the player always starts even if preferences are slow to load.\n\nPreviously in 2.6 and earlier\n\n- Three-mode CAS Enhance toggle (NEW adaptive, OLD classic 2.0, OFF).\n- Default refresh rate 72 Hz on all devices (user can switch in Settings).\n- 'Remember Settings' OFF by default \u2014 opt in for persistence.\n- Mirror mode fixed for 3D SBS (stereo depth no longer inverted).\n- Multi-video buffer optimized \u2014 SBS primary no longer stutters.\n- Refresh rate setting (72/80/90/120 Hz, options per device).\n- 16x anisotropic filtering and 2x MSAA for crisper VR rendering.\n- Discord community block in the file browser sidebar.", "created_date": 1779745969, "id": "28147896118144108", "version": "2.8", "version_code": 21, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "27125292497071147", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "28147896118144108"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1252765963588051"}]}, "change_log": "What's New in 2.7\n\nCritical Fix\n- Fixed a hang where the player would never start a video after enabling 'Remember Settings' and restarting the app. Settings load and rendering pipeline are now decoupled, so the player always starts even if preferences are slow to load. 2-second timeout + factory-defaults fallback added as safety net.\n\nPreviously in 2.6\n\nImage Quality\n- Factory default is now neutral (matches Reset Enhance) - no PhotoReal auto-applied to any video. Previously PhotoReal was over-sharpening lower-quality content. You can still pick PhotoReal manually in the Enhance panel.\n\nPerformance\n- Faster startup: settings are now bulk-read in a single snapshot from DataStore (was 15+ sequential reads).\n\nPreviously in 2.4\n\nImage Quality\n- CAS Enhance now has THREE modes (cycle by tapping the button in the Enhance panel):\n  * NEW (green, default) - adaptive Catmull-Rom bicubic for upscaling, multi-tap box filter for downscaling\n  * OLD (orange) - classic 2.0 sharpening with anti-ringing clamp, softer character\n  * OFF (gray) - pure hardware bilinear, no post-processing\n\nSettings\n- Default refresh rate is now 72 Hz on all devices (was 120 Hz)\n- 'Remember Settings' is now OFF by default - player resets to factory defaults each session unless you opt in", "created_date": 1778542572, "id": "27973216458945409", "version": "2.7", "version_code": 20, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "27125292497071147", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "28147896118144108"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1252765963588051"}]}, "change_log": "What's New in 2.6\n\nImage Quality\n- Factory default is now neutral (matches Reset Enhance) - no PhotoReal auto-applied to any video. Previously PhotoReal was over-sharpening lower-quality content. You can still pick PhotoReal manually in the Enhance panel.\n\nPerformance\n- Faster startup: settings are now bulk-read in a single snapshot from DataStore (was 15+ sequential reads). Fixes the stutter that appeared on the second video when 'Remember Settings' was enabled.\n\nPreviously in 2.4\n\nImage Quality\n- CAS Enhance now has THREE modes (cycle by tapping the button in the Enhance panel):\n  * NEW (green, default) - adaptive Catmull-Rom bicubic for upscaling, multi-tap box filter for downscaling\n  * OLD (orange) - classic 2.0 sharpening with anti-ringing clamp, softer character\n  * OFF (gray) - pure hardware bilinear, no post-processing\n\nSettings\n- Default refresh rate is now 72 Hz on all devices (was 120 Hz)\n- 'Remember Settings' is now OFF by default - player resets to factory defaults each session unless you opt in", "created_date": 1778541316, "id": "27973048818962173", "version": "2.6", "version_code": 19, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "27125292497071147", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "28147896118144108"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1252765963588051"}]}, "change_log": "What's New in 2.4\n\nImage Quality\n- CAS Enhance now has THREE modes (cycle by tapping the button in the Enhance panel):\n  * NEW (green, default) - adaptive Catmull-Rom bicubic for upscaling, multi-tap box filter for downscaling\n  * OLD (orange) - classic 2.0 sharpening with anti-ringing clamp, softer character\n  * OFF (gray) - pure hardware bilinear, no post-processing\n- PhotoReal is now applied as the factory default color profile on fresh install (was auto-applied only for VR 180 before)\n- PhotoReal sharpness restored to 0.40 (no halos on flat 2D content)\n\nSettings\n- Default refresh rate is now 72 Hz on all devices (was 120 Hz). User can switch in Settings.\n- 'Remember Settings' is now OFF by default - the player resets to factory defaults each session unless you explicitly opt in\n\nPreviously in 2.3\n\nImage Quality\n- Mirror mode fixed for 3D SBS content - eyes are now properly swapped, so stereo depth is no longer inverted when mirroring\n\nPerformance\n- Multi-video mode: optimized buffer allocation - the primary 3D SBS video gets a larger buffer, the two flat videos get smaller buffers. Less heap pressure overall and the SBS stream no longer stutters\n\nFixes\n- Exiting Settings: tabs and sort buttons now properly restore when switching directly from Settings to Internal Memory or USB OTG", "created_date": 1778505759, "id": "27967319832868405", "version": "2.4", "version_code": 17, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "27125292497071147", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "28147896118144108"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "1252765963588051"}]}, "change_log": "What's New in 2.3\n\nImage Quality\n- Mirror mode fixed for 3D SBS content - eyes are now properly swapped, so stereo depth is no longer inverted when mirroring\n\nPerformance\n- Multi-video mode: optimized buffer allocation - the primary 3D SBS video gets a larger buffer, the two flat videos get smaller buffers. Less heap pressure overall and the SBS stream no longer stutters\n\nFixes\n- Exiting Settings: tabs and sort buttons now properly restore when switching directly from Settings to Internal Memory or USB OTG\n\nPreviously in 2.2\n\nImage Quality\n- Adaptive video filtering: Catmull-Rom bicubic for upscaling, multi-tap box filter for downscaling - noticeably sharper 4K SBS, less aliasing on 8K SBS\n- 16x anisotropic filtering for crisp 180/360 sphere edges\n- 2x MSAA anti-aliasing on geometry and menu edges\n\nRefresh Rate\n- New Refresh Rate setting (72/80/90/120 Hz) - options adapt to your Quest device\n- Default is now 120 Hz on supported devices\n- Live refresh rate indicator shown in the bottom bar\n\nSettings\n- Player settings (CAS, color, mirror, swap eyes, smooth, etc.) now persist between videos and sessions\n- New 'Remember Settings' Yes/No toggle\n- Cleaner Settings view - tabs/sort/search hidden while adjusting preferences\n\nFixes\n- Thumbnails resume loading after returning from playback\n- No more false 'No USB device detected' message when quickly switching sources\n- Refresh rate no longer resets to 72 Hz after session start", "created_date": 1778270840, "id": "27935347749398947", "version": "2.3", "version_code": 16, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": null, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}]}}, "viewer": {"user": null}}}